course: dictionary
lesson: 8974
title: Words that wind and twist
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word like sinuous can look hard, but the sentence around it gives you clues. «This sleek, sinuous, full-bodied animal, chasing and chuckling» is the Mole's view of a river. A river that chases and chuckles is moving, so sinuous must describe the way it moves and bends.
explain: Think about what a snake looks like as it moves: its body curves from side to side. Sinuous means curving and winding, with many bends, like a snake or a river.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «winding» in place of sinuous: «this sleek, winding, full-bodied animal, chasing and chuckling» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The word can also describe smooth, twisting, graceful movement, like the way an eel moves through water.
fact: Sinuous means curving and winding, with many bends.
fact: Sinuous can describe a river, a road, or a snake.
fact: Sinuous also means moving in a smooth, twisting, graceful way.
fact: Sinuous is an adjective: more sinuous, most sinuous.
fact: Snakes and eels move in sinuous waves.
exercise: «The sinuous river wound through the valley.» What does sinuous mean here? | Straight and flat | *Curving and winding, with many bends | Very loud and noisy | Frozen solid
exercise: Which of these moves in sinuous waves? | A parked car | A clock | *A snake | A brick wall
exercise: Find and copy the word from «this sleek, sinuous, full-bodied animal, chasing and chuckling» that means curving and winding. | full-bodied | *sinuous | sleek | chasing
test: The Mole was «bewitched, entranced, fascinated» by the river, which seemed to him «this sleek, sinuous, full-bodied animal». What does sinuous tell us about the river? | It is very cold | *Its shape winds and bends, like a snake | It is standing still | It is made of sand
test: Which phrase uses sinuous to mean moving in a smooth, twisting, graceful way? | The dancer stamped and shouted | The dancer forgot the steps | *The dancer's arms moved in sinuous curves | The dancer was sitting down
exam: Which word best fits? «The eel swam through the water in ___ waves.» | *Sinuous | Curt | Barely | Luminous
